nd Piran municipality identities. Use authoritative definitions and complete-source parent/child geometry evidence; produce explicit tier and crosswalk recommendations or restoration instructions.\n\n## Exact parent IDs (17)\n\n- `framework:province:ankaran-ancarano:3995388bc628`\n- `framework:province:bor-district:bcc3f7cd47cb`\n- `framework:province:branicevo-district:8cca74a50478`\n- `framework:province:izola-isola:bc2149bec285`\n- `framework:province:jablanica-district:e84aa5c8e2dd`\n- `framework:province:nisava-district:ac978fa5e54b`\n- `framework:province:pcinja-district:c70e78a0f661`\n- `framework:province:piran-pirano:1d929956088b`\n- `framework:province:pirot-district:ce075dca01df`\n- `framework:province:podunavlje-district:2b58b07c63e8`\n- `framework:province:pomoravlje-district:21d27b2672d2`\n- `framework:province:rasina-district:e0e6fad35903`\n- `framework:province:south-banat-district:b205db771f84`\n- `framework:province:toplica-district:05291e06d303`\n- `framework:province:vzhodna:d0d1788c155c`\n- `framework:province:zahodna-slovenija:52f5c9765039`\n- `framework:province:zajecar-district:9380a7a06e84`\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Document every one of the 17 parent IDs, its complete scoped child set, official geographic role, source vintage/license, and whether the available evidence supports full-parent completeness.\n- Compare the Serbian district parents with Slovenia’s official 12 NUTS3 statistical regions and two NUTS2 cohesion regions; do not treat the tiers as interchangeable solely because Atlas calls them `province`.\n- Resolve the three municipality-duplicating coastal parent records against authoritative GURS/administrative definitions and source polygon compatibility, including neighboring granularity.\n- Retain complete lawful source geometry or restoration instructions, hashes and reproducible methods. Recommend only evidence-backed, ID-preserving hierarchy/geometry work; explicitly preserve unresolved boundary/completeness limits. No shared geography edits or regional approval.\n\n## Evidence and limits\n\nThe exact parent list and child sets are in `data/regional-review/regional-review-d282e62cf0209796/province-assessments.json`; unit and source evidence is in the same #423 owned packet. #423 leaves these parent-tier and singleton questions unresolved.\n\nAll outcomes are research findings, not geographic approval or authorization to publish/import. Preserve existing packet sources, release pins, identities, and other workers’ evidence.\n\n<!-- worldatlas-work:v1\n{\"max_prs\":1,\"depends_on\":[423],\"scope\":\"Assess the 17 exact Atlas province-parent records and the 278 locations scoped in #423. Reconcile Serbian district-tier parents with Slovenia’s cohesion/statistical-region parents and the three singleton coastal parent records that duplicate Ankaran, Izola and Piran municipality identities. Use authoritative definitions and complete-source parent/child geometry evidence; produce explicit tier and crosswalk recommendations or restoration instructions.\",\"mode\":\"geography\",\"owned_paths\":[\"data/regional-review/followup-yugoslavia-423-parent-tiers-20261005/\"],\"evidence_quality\":{\"version\":1,\"manifest_path\":\"data/regional-review/followup-yugoslavia-423-parent-tiers-20261005/evidence-quality.json\",\"subject_ids\":[\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B14333994307421\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B14779468402484\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B15135122038739\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B16465002195595\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B17937032447528\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B18327581352007\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B19679900435135\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B20144480687760\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B21672557682784\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B2646840905075\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B26895263090033\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B29190623105772\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B30948132867080\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B31931832207402\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B34776853271491\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B3832179946279\",\"gb:SRB:ADM2:33768554B39192124193600\",\"gb:SRB